:INFO
Art. 3b Use of products and substances in accordance with Article 16j para paragraph 2 letter b and c of the Organic Farming Ordinance in the production of wine
Products and substances in accordance with Annex V Part D of Implementing Regulation (EU) 2021/1165 may be used for the production of wine.
|

:NOTE
Art. 3b — Inserted by No I of the EAER O of 31 Oct. 2012 (AS 2012 6357). Amended by No I of the EAER O of 3 Nov. 2020, in force since 1 Jan. 2022 (AS 2021 683).
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2021/1165 of 15 July 2021 authorising certain products and substances for use in organic production and establishing their lists, OJ L 253 of 16.7.2021, p. 45–47.
|

:INFO
Art. 3c Oenological practices and processes and restrictions thereon
Oenological practices and processes in accordance with Annex II Part VI number 3 of Regulation (EU) 2018/848 as amended by Annex 3b are permitted.
|

:NOTE
Art. 3c — Inserted by No I of the EAER O of 31 Oct. 2012 (AS 2012 6357). Amended by No I of the EAER O of 3 Nov. 2020, in force since 1 Jan. 2022 (AS 2021 683).
|

:INFO
Art. 3d Practices and processes for the production of processed organic foodstuffs
Ion exchange und adsorption resin processes are only permitted:
a. for the preparation of foodstuffs for persons with special dietary requirements in accordance with Article 2 letters a–c SDRO;
b. for the partial deacidification of pear juice for the production of pear juice concentrate with an acidity of 6–12 g malic acid/kg and a Brix value of 80–82° Brix, intended exclusively for the Swiss market
|

:NOTE
Art. 3d — Inserted by No I of the EAER O of 2 Nov. 2022 (AS 2022 733). Amended by No I of the EAER O of 29 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 716).
